all of show developer peter lenkov's  reboots of previous tv shows including  macgyver magnum pi and hawaii 5-0 share  the same fictional universe known as the  lenkav verse and have been substantial  hits for their parent network cbs  however the length of verse has seen a  great deal of controversy over the years  in 2017 regular hawaii five-o cast  members daniel day kim and grace park  left the series over a salary dispute  given how they were reportedly paid 10  to 15 percent less than series leads  alex o'laughlin and scott khan then in  2020 lenkov was fired from the three  shows by cbs after multiple claims that  he'd fostered a toxic work environment  as well as allegations that he was  abusive and manipulative on sets  nevertheless hawaii 5.0 did wrap up a  successful 240 episode run while  macgyver concluded in 2021 after five  seasons and magnum is still on the air  as of 2022 much of this of course is  behind the scenes stuff and even really  tense sets have been known to produce  entertaining works on the whole hawaii  five-o is precisely the kind of  action-packed police procedural drama  that's an easy fit for a multiple season  run however that doesn't mean the show  is entirely devoid of problematic  moments in front of the camera in fact  all those off-screen problems might have  meant that nobody noticed how bleak and  off-putting a particular season 10  plotters let's take a look at the hawaii  5.0 scene that the fans think went too  far in episode 14 of season 10 dany  meets an attractive woman at a bar and  they hit it off however as they head  home together the pair end up in a crash  after dany is forced to swerve to avoid  an oncoming car the woman is badly  injured and they're in a remote area  without cell reception dramatic and sad  scenes ensue and in the end she passes  away before help arrives without ever  telling the devastated dany her name  oh it's so crazy so funny i could i got  the luck like you said i meet the girl  in my dreams i get in a car accident  the plot is definitely sad but it  arguably feels off in a number of ways  chief among them is the fact that the  entire thing seems to run against dany's  characterization which is saying  something considering that the show's  had time to explore the character for  years and years at this point while dany  is incredibly faithful to his friends  he's also a rather melancholic and  reserved figure who's incredibly  unlikely to open the creaky armor of his  sarcastic exterior for a new  acquaintance as such it seems out of  character for dany to bond with someone  so quickly and unfair to have the  character go through another loss after  the murder of his partner and a messy  divorce this may be one of the reasons  why some fans feel the story is  contrived one hawaii 5-0 subreddit user  pointed out dany's out of character  behavior and felt that the storyline  only happened as quote another go for  peter lenkov to punish the character  as a whole the episode is clearly not a  fan favorite episode in fact with this  comparatively mega 6.8 imdb user rating  it's far and away the lowest rated  episode in the entire hawaii 5-0 season  10. apart from the way the episode both  portrays dany in a strange way and puts  him through the emotional ringer by  introducing a potential love interest  and taking her away within the span of a  single episode's run time viewers have  pointed out other issues in the episode  as well  multiple imdb user reviews concurred  that dany's behavior is off here and not  only in the dramatic death scene one  user pointed out that his first aid  skills are completely wrong and even  said that he directly contributes to the  woman's fate with his clumsy attempts to  save her what's more another user noted  that the terrifying incident is more or  less forgotten after the episode is over  since quote the police did not  investigate or judge the driver and they  never mention it again  come on come on come on come on  come on  come on  somebody  while scott khan gets a chance to flex  his dramatic muscles here his  character's big scene in this episode  has clearly bothered many people as has  a whole bunch of other stuff surrounding  it all in all definitely not the finest  hour of hawaii 5-0  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  your favorite awkward television moments  are coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one  [Music]
 

